<http://www.reuters.com/article/2014/10/10/us-usa-california-mountains-idUSKCN0HZ0U720141010> <http://ontology.ontotext.com/publishing#genericJson> "{\"id\":\"http://www.reuters.com/article/2014/10/10/us-usa-california-mountains-idUSKCN0HZ0U720141010\",\"feature-set\":[],\"document-parts\":{\"feature-set\":[{\"name\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"name\":\"isDebugMode\"},\"value\":{\"type\":\"XS_BOOLEAN\",\"value\":\"true\"}},{\"name\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"name\":\"sentimentScore\"},\"value\":{\"type\":\"XS_DOUBLE\",\"value\":\"0.5533740100214285\"}},{\"name\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"name\":\"summary\"},\"value\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"value\":\"Obama to declare Los Angeles-area mountains national monument | Reuters\"}},{\"name\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"name\":\"title\"},\"value\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"value\":\"Obama to declare Los Angeles-area mountains national monument\"}},{\"name\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"name\":\"encoding\"},\"value\":{\"type\":\"XS_STRING\",\"value\":\"UTF-8\"}}],\"document-part\":[{\"feature-set\":[],\"id\":\"0\",\"part\":\"ALL\",\"content\":{\"text\":\"Obama to declare Los Angeles-area mountains national monument | Reuters\\n\\n\\nObama to declare Los Angeles-area mountains national monument\\n\\nBy Sharon Bernstein\\n\\n(Reuters) - President Barack Obama will declare a swath of the San Gabriel Mountains near Los Angeles as a national monument on Friday, the White House said, following an 11-year effort that got caught up in partisan politics.\\n\\nAlong with the designation, the U.S. Forest Service will dedicate $1 million in educational staff, graffiti removal and other long-deferred maintenance work, and non-profit foundations have committed an additional $3.5 million for restoration and stewardship of mountain areas.\\n\\nThe declaration is being made at the request of Democratic Representative Judy Chu, whose legislation to protect the area is stuck in Congress along with other wilderness bills as Republicans and Democrats feud.\\n\\nThe 540-square-mile (1,400-square-km) section of the Angeles National Forest to be protected under the order attracts 3 million visitors a year, but graffiti mars the landscape, and the U.S. Forest Service has little money for signage or even restroom repair, said Chu, whose district includes part of the area.\\n\\nLegislation to protect the mountains has been introduced twice in Congress, once in 2003, leading to a 10-year-study by the U.S. Park Service, and then in June 2014, when Chu submitted a bill to designate them a national recreation area.\\n\\nAfter her bill became stuck in a subcommittee, Chu asked Obama to use his executive authority to declare part of the area a national monument.\\n\\nThat angered some local officials and many Republicans, who said it was an end-run around Congress.\\n\\nJudy Nelson, mayor of the foothill city of Glendora, said naming the area a national monument instead of a national recreation area could invoke different environmental protection rules and might harm businesses.\\n\\nObama's declaration will affect only land already designated as a national forest, and will not include San Bernardino County, whose governing body voted to oppose the action.\\n\\n(Reporting by Sharon Bernstein in Sacramento, Calif.; Editing by Peter Cooney )\\n\",\"node\":[{\"id\":\"0\",\"offset\":0},{\"id\":\"5\",\"offset\":5},{\"id\":\"17\",\"offset\":17},{\"id\":\"28\",\"offset\":28},{\"id\":\"29\",\"offset\":29},{\"id\":\"33\",\"offset\":33},{\"id\":\"34\",\"offset\":34},{\"id\":\"43\",\"offset\":43},{\"id\":\"44\",\"offset\":44},{\"id\":\"61\",\"offset\":61},{\"id\":\"64\",\"offset\":64},{\"id\":\"71\",\"offset\":71},{\"id\":\"74\",\"offset\":74},{\"id\":\"79\",\"offset\":79},{\"id\":\"91\",\"offset\":91},{\"id\":\"102\",\"offset\":102},{\"id\":\"103\",\"offset\":103},{\"id\":\"107\",\"offset\":107},{\"id\":\"108\",\"offset\":108},{\"id\":\"117\",\"offset\":117},{\"id\":\"118\",\"offset\":118},{\"id\":\"135\",\"offset\":135},{\"id\":\"1