<http://data.ontotext.com/publishing/RelationPersonQuotation/_of_the_unique_things_about_him_one_is_of_course_his_style_which_is_very_precise_very_economical_he_writes_small_short_very_elegant_sentences_englund_said_and_he_returns_to_generally_the_same_topics_again_and_again_simply_because_these_topics_cannot_be_exhausted_> <http://ontology.ontotext.com/taxonomy/relationText> "\"Of the unique things about him, one is of course his style which is very precise, very economical. He writes small, short, very elegant sentences. And he returns to generally the same topics again and again, simply because these topics cannot be exhausted.\"" .
<http://data.ontotext.com/publishing/RelationPersonQuotation/_after_each_novel_i_have_the_impression_that_i_have_cleared_it_all_away_modiano_told_france_today_in_a_2011_interview_but_i_know_i_ll_come_back_over_and_over_again_to_tiny_details_little_things_that_are_part_of_what_i_am_> <http://ontology.ontotext.com/taxonomy/relationText> "\"After each novel, I have the impression that I have cleared it all away. But I know I'll come back over and over again to tiny details, little things that are part of what I am.\"" .
